    "text": "In an operating system with virtual memory, the number of entries in an **Inverted Page Table** is equal to:",
    "options": [
      "The number of pages in the virtual address space of all processes combined.",
      "The number of page frames in physical main memory.",
      "The number of processes currently active in the system.",
      "The size of virtual memory divided by page size."
    ],
    "answer": 1,
    "explanation": "### Inverted Page Table Architecture:\n- In a traditional page table, each process has its own page table with one entry per virtual page.\n- In an **Inverted Page Table**, there is only **one global page table** for the entire system.\n- Each entry in the inverted page table corresponds to exactly **one physical frame of main memory**.\n- Hence, the number of entries in an Inverted Page Table is strictly equal to the **number of frames in physical memory**.",
    "source": "GATE CSE 2015 Shift 2 Q41",
    "year": 2015,
    "verified": true,
    "difficulty": 1
