    "explanation": "### Definition and Mechanism of Thrashing:\n- When the sum of the working sets of all active processes exceeds the total available physical memory frames, processes continually page fault.\n- The operating system spends almost all of its time servicing page faults (swapping pages into and out of disk), causing CPU utilization to plummet to near zero.\n- This catastrophic condition is called **Thrashing**.",
