    "text": "In the standard First Readers-Writers solution (Readers-preference) using semaphores `mutex` and `wrt` (both initialized to $1$) and integer `readcount` (initialized to $0$):\\n\\n```c\\n// Reader:\\nP(mutex);\\nreadcount++;\\nif (readcount == 1)\\n    P(wrt);\\nV(mutex);\\n\\n/* Reading occurs */\\n\\nP(mutex);\\nreadcount--;\\nif (readcount == 0)\\n    V(wrt);\\nV(mutex);\\n```\\n\\nWhich of the following describes the susceptibility to starvation in this implementation?",
