    "explanation": "**Step-by-step Ticket Lock Behavior:**\\n- When 8 threads call `acquire()`, each thread receives a unique consecutive ticket from $0$ to $7$ via atomic `FetchAndAdd`, and `ticket` becomes $8$.\\n- Thread with `my_ticket == 0` immediately enters the CS because `turn == 0`.\\n- Upon exiting CS, thread 0 calls `release()`, which increments `turn` from $0$ to $1$.\\n- This wakes thread with ticket 1, which enters, finishes, and increments `turn` from $1$ to $2$, and so on.\\n- Each thread calls `release()` exactly once, incrementing `turn` exactly once.\\n- After all 8 threads finish their critical sections, `turn` is incremented exactly $8$ times (final `turn = 8`).",
    "text": "A ticket lock implementation uses atomic `FetchAndAdd(int *var, int val)`:\\n\\n```c\\ntypedef struct {\\n    int ticket;\\n    int turn;\\n} ticket_lock_t;\\n\\nvoid acquire(ticket_lock_t *lock) {\\n    int my_ticket = FetchAndAdd(&lock->ticket, 1);\\n    while (lock->turn != my_ticket);\\n}\\n\\nvoid release(ticket_lock_t *lock) {\\n    lock->turn++;\\n}\\n```\\n\\nInitially, `ticket = 0` and `turn = 0`. If 8 threads concurrently call `acquire()`, what is the maximum number of times the variable `turn` is incremented after all 8 threads complete their critical sections and call `release()`?",
