    "answer": 0,
    "explanation": "**Step 1: Check conditions for $P_1$'s request:**\\n- $\\text{Request}(P_1) = (1, 1, 1, 0)$.\\n- $\\text{Need}(P_1) = (2, 2, 2, 1) \\implies (1, 1, 1, 0) \\le (2, 2, 2, 1)$ (Valid).\\n- $\\text{Available} = (2, 3, 3, 2) \\implies (1, 1, 1, 0) \\le (2, 3, 3, 2)$ (Valid).\\n\\n**Step 2: Pretend to allocate:**\\n- $\\text{New Available} = (2, 3, 3, 2) - (1, 1, 1, 0) = (1, 2, 2, 2)$.\\n- $\\text{New Allocation}(P_1) = (2, 1, 0, 1) + (1, 1, 1, 0) = (3, 2, 1, 1)$.\\n- $\\text{New Need}(P_1) = (2, 2, 2, 1) - (1, 1, 1, 0) = (1, 1, 1, 1)$.\\n\\n**Step 3: Run Safety Algorithm on new state:**\\n- Available $= (1, 2, 2, 2)$.\\n- Can $P_3$ execute? $\\text{Need}(P_3) = (1, 2, 2, 1) \\le (1, 2, 2, 2) \\implies$ **Yes!**\\n  - New Available $= (1, 2, 2, 2) + (1, 2, 1, 1) = (2, 4, 3, 3)$.\\n- Can $P_1$ execute? $\\text{Need}(P_1) = (1, 1, 1, 1) \\le (2, 4, 3, 3) \\implies$ **Yes!**\\n  - New Available $= (2, 4, 3, 3) + (3, 2, 1, 1) = (5, 6, 4, 4)$.\\n- Can $P_0, P_2, P_4$ execute? All needs are $\\le (5, 6, 4, 4)$.\\n- A valid safe sequence $\\langle P_3, P_1, P_0, P_2, P_4 \\rangle$ exists! Hence the request is safely granted immediately.",
