    "explanation": "**Step 1: Calculate block pointer capacity per disk block.**\\n- Block size $= 4\\text{ KB} = 4096\\text{ bytes}$.\\n- Pointer size $= 4\\text{ bytes}$.\\n- Pointers per indirect block $K = \\frac{4096}{4} = 1024 = 2^{10}$.\\n\\n**Step 2: Calculate data blocks addressable by each pointer type.**\\n- **Direct pointers**: $12 \\times 1 = 12$ data blocks $= 12 \\times 4\\text{ KB} = 48\\text{ KB}$.\\n- **Single indirect**: $1 \\times K = 1024$ data blocks $= 1024 \\times 4\\text{ KB} = 4\\text{ MB}$.\\n- **Double indirect**: $1 \\times K^2 = 1024^2 = 2^{20}$ data blocks $= 2^{20} \\times 4\\text{ KB} = 4\\text{ GB}$.\\n- **Triple indirect**: $1 \\times K^3 = (2^{10})^3 = 2^{30}$ data blocks $= 2^{30} \\times 4\\text{ KB} = 4\\text{ TB} = 4096\\text{ GB}$.\\n\\n**Step 3: Total maximum file size.**\\n$$\\text{Total} = 48\\text{ KB} + 4\\text{ MB} + 4\\text{ GB} + 4096\\text{ GB} \\approx 4096\\text{ GB} + 4.004\\text{ GB} \\approx 4100\\text{ GB}$$\\n- More precisely: $4096 + 4 = 4100\\text{ GB}$ (to nearest integer: 4100).",
