    "explanation": "**Step 1: Calculate pointers per block.**\\n- Block size $= 8\\text{ KB} = 2^{13}\\text{ bytes}$.\\n- Pointer size $= 8\\text{ bytes} = 2^3\\text{ bytes}$.\\n- Pointers per block $K = \\frac{2^{13}}{2^3} = 2^{10} = 1024$.\\n\\n**Step 2: Capacity by pointer type.**\\n- Direct: $8 \\times 8\\text{ KB} = 64\\text{ KB}$.\\n- 2 Single indirect: $2 \\times 1024 \\times 8\\text{ KB} = 2048 \\times 8\\text{ KB} = 16\\text{ MB}$.\\n- 1 Double indirect: $1 \\times 1024^2 \\times 8\\text{ KB} = 2^{20} \\times 8\\text{ KB} = 8\\text{ GB}$.\\n- 1 Triple indirect: $1 \\times 1024^3 \\times 8\\text{ KB} = 2^{30} \\times 8\\text{ KB} = 8\\text{ TB}$.\\n\\n**Step 3: Total Size.**\\n$$\\text{Total} = 8\\text{ TB} + 8\\text{ GB} + 16\\text{ MB} + 64\\text{ KB} \\approx 8\\text{ TB}$$",
    "text": "A 64-bit operating system uses $8\\text{ KB}$ disk blocks with $8\\text{-byte}$ ($64\\text{-bit}$) block pointers. The inode contains 8 direct, 2 single indirect, 1 double indirect, and 1 triple indirect pointer.\\n\\nWhat is the maximum file size expressible in Terabytes ($1\\text{ TB} = 2^{40}\\text{ bytes}$)? (Round to nearest integer).",
    "source": "GATE High-Yield Model"
