    "text": "In a Unix file system, the root directory `/` is located at known inode 2. A process opens the file `/usr/bin/local/gcc`. Assume each directory (`/`, `usr`, `bin`, `local`) fits in exactly one disk block, and the file `gcc` is a small file fitting in 1 data block.\\n\\nIf initially no inodes or directory blocks are present in memory/buffer cache, how many total disk block reads (including inode table blocks and directory/file data blocks) are required to read the first byte of `gcc`? (Assume each inode lookup requires 1 disk read to fetch its inode structure from the inode table).",
