    "answer": 0,
    "explanation": "### HDLC Bit-Stuffing Step-by-Step Derivation:\n1. **Rule**: A `0` is stuffed immediately after every run of five consecutive `1`s in the payload data.\n2. **Input Stream Analysis**:\n   - Start: `0 1 1 0` (two 1s)\n   - Next run of 1s: `1 1 1 1 1` (five 1s) $\\implies$ **STUFF `0`** $\\implies$ becomes `111110`\n   - Next remaining bits: `1 1 0` (two 1s followed by 0)\n   - Next run of 1s: `1 1 1 1 1` (five 1s) $\\implies$ **STUFF `0`** $\\implies$ becomes `111110`\n   - Next remaining bits: `0 1 1 0` (two 1s)\n3. **Combining all stuffed chunks**:\n   - `0110` + `11111` + `[0]` + `110` + `11111` + `[0]` + `0110`\n   - $= \\text{`01101111101101111100110`}$\n\nThus, Option A is correct.\n\n**⚠️ Exam Trap**: Even if the 6th bit in the original stream was a `1` or `0`, the stuffing occurs strictly after the 5th consecutive `1`.",
