    "explanation": "### IPv4 vs IPv6 Header Differences:\n- In IPv6, the **Header Checksum** field was completely removed because Layer 2 (Ethernet CRC) and Layer 4 (TCP/UDP checksums) already provide robust error checking. Eliminating checksum re-computation at every hop drastically reduces router processing overhead.\n- In addition, fragmentation fields (Identification, Flags, Fragment Offset) were moved to optional extension headers.\n\nThus, Option A is correct.\n\n**⚠️ Exam Trap**: IPv6 replaced TTL with 'Hop Limit' and Protocol with 'Next Header', but eliminated Header Checksum entirely.",
