    "explanation": "**Step 1: Probability of success and failure.**\n- $P_{\\text{succ}} = (1 - p)(1 - q) = (0.92)(0.95) = 0.874$.\n- $P_{\\text{fail}} = 1 - 0.874 = 0.126$.\n\n**Step 2: Expected time per packet.**\n- Time on success: $T_{\\text{succ}} = T_t + 2T_p = 2 + 36 = 38\\text{ ms}$.\n- Time on failure: $T_{\\text{out}} = 50\\text{ ms}$.\n- Expected failures before success $= \\frac{P_{\\text{fail}}}{P_{\\text{succ}}} = \\frac{0.126}{0.874} \\approx 0.144165$.\n- $E[T_{\\text{pkt}}] = 38 + (0.144165 \\times 50) = 38 + 7.2082 = 45.2082\\text{ ms}$.\n\n**Step 3: Total time for 500 packets.**\n- $T_{\\text{total}} = 500 \\times 45.2082\\text{ ms} = 22604.1\\text{ ms} = 22.60\\text{ seconds}$.",
    "text": "A sender transmits $M = 500$ packets using the Stop-and-Wait ARQ protocol.\n- Packet transmission time $T_t = 2\\text{ ms}$, one-way propagation delay $T_p = 18\\text{ ms}$.\n- ACK transmission time is negligible.\n- Timeout interval is set to $T_{\\text{out}} = 50\\text{ ms}$ (measured from the start of packet transmission).\n- The forward packet loss probability is $p = 0.08$.\n- The reverse ACK loss probability is $q = 0.05$.\n- Packet and ACK losses are mutually independent.\n\nCalculate the total expected time (in seconds, rounded to two decimal places) required to successfully deliver all $500$ packets to the receiver.",
