    "explanation": "### Ratio Test for Asymptotic Comparison:\nCompute the limit $\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\frac{f(n)}{g(n)}$:\n$$\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\frac{n^2 \\log n}{n^{2.5}} = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\frac{\\log n}{n^{0.5}}$$\nUsing L'Hôpital's Rule:\n$$\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\frac{1/n}{0.5 n^{-0.5}} = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{n}} = 0$$\nSince the limit is $0$, $f(n) = o(g(n))$, which implies $f(n) = O(g(n))$.\n\nHence, option (A) is correct."
