    "explanation": "### Radix Sort with Base $n$:\n- Range of numbers is $0$ to $n^2 - 1$.\n- In base $b = n$, each number has $d = \\log_b(n^2) = \\log_n(n^2) = 2$ digits.\n- Each digit takes values in $\\{0, 1, \\dots, n-1\\}$.\n- Running stable Counting Sort on $n$ numbers with digits in range $[0, n-1]$ takes $\\Theta(n + b) = \\Theta(n + n) = \\Theta(n)$ time per digit.\n- Since there are $d = 2$ digits, total time complexity is $d \\times \\Theta(n + b) = 2 \\times \\Theta(n) = \\Theta(n)$.\n\nHence, option (A) is correct."
