    "explanation": "### Kruskal's Algorithm Complexity Breakdown:\n1. Sorting the $E$ edges by weight: $\\Theta(E \\log E) = \\Theta(E \\log V^2) = \\Theta(E \\log V)$.\n2. Performing $|V|$ `Make-Set` operations and $2|E|$ `Find-Set` / `Union` operations using DSU with union-by-rank and path compression takes $O(E \\cdot \\alpha(V))$ time, where $\\alpha(V)$ is the extremely slow-growing inverse Ackermann function.\n3. The bottleneck step is sorting the edges: $\\Theta(E \\log V)$.\n\nThus, the total time complexity is $\\Theta(E \\log V)$, which is option (B)."
