    "text": "In a Huffman tree constructed for a set of characters, the character $x$ has the lowest frequency among all characters. What is the MAXIMUM possible difference between the depth of the leaf node corresponding to $x$ and the depth of the leaf node corresponding to the character with the highest frequency in a tree with 4 characters?",
    "answer": 2,
    "explanation": "### Huffman Tree Topology for 4 Characters:\n- For $n = 4$ characters, a Huffman tree can have two possible shapes:\n  1. Fully balanced (complete binary tree): 4 leaves at depth 2 (difference $= 2 - 2 = 0$).\n  2. Highly skewed (caterpillar tree): lowest frequency character is at depth 3, second lowest at depth 3, third lowest at depth 2, and highest frequency character at depth 1.\n- In the skewed tree, the highest frequency character is at depth 1, and the lowest frequency character $x$ is at depth 3.\n- The maximum difference in depth $= 3 - 1 = 2$."
