    "text": "Find the minimum number of scalar multiplications required to multiply four matrices $A_1, A_2, A_3, A_4$ with dimensions $10 \\times 100$, $100 \\times 5$, $5 \\times 50$, and $50 \\times 1$ respectively.",
    "answer": 1750,
    "explanation": "### Matrix Chain Multiplication Dynamic Programming:\n- Dimension array: $p = [10, 100, 5, 50, 1]$ where $A_1: 10\\times 100, A_2: 100\\times 5, A_3: 5\\times 50, A_4: 50\\times 1$.\n- Chains of length 2:\n  - $m[1,2] = 10 \\times 100 \\times 5 = 5000$\n  - $m[2,3] = 100 \\times 5 \\times 50 = 25000$\n  - $m[3,4] = 5 \\times 50 \\times 1 = 250$\n- Chains of length 3:\n  - $m[1,3] = \\min(m[1,1]+m[2,3]+10\\times 100\\times 50, m[1,2]+m[3,3]+10\\times 5\\times 50) = \\min(0+25000+50000, 5000+0+2500) = 7500$ (split at $k=2$).\n  - $m[2,4] = \\min(m[2,2]+m[3,4]+100\\times 5\\times 1, m[2,3]+m[4,4]+100\\times 50\\times 1) = \\min(0+250+500, 25000+0+5000) = 750$ (split at $k=2$, i.e. $A_2(A_3 A_4)$).\n- Chains of length 4 ($m[1,4]$):\n  - $k=1: m[1,1] + m[2,4] + 10\\times 100\\times 1 = 0 + 750 + 1000 = 1750$\n  - $k=2: m[1,2] + m[3,4] + 10\\times 5\\times 1 = 5000 + 250 + 50 = 5300$\n  - $k=3: m[1,3] + m[4,4] + 10\\times 50\\times 1 = 7500 + 0 + 500 = 8000$\n- Optimal cost $= \\min(1750, 5300, 8000) = 1750$.\nParenthesization: $A_1(A_2(A_3 A_4))$."
