    "explanation": "**Held-Karp Analysis:**\n1. **State Space:** There are $2^n$ subsets $S \\subseteq V$. For each subset of size $k$, the last visited vertex $u \\in S$ can be any of the $k$ vertices. Thus the total number of states is $\\sum_{k=1}^n \\binom{n}{k} k = n 2^{n-1} = \\Theta(n 2^n)$.\n2. **Transitions:** For each state $(S, u)$, we iterate over all possible preceding vertices $v \\in S \\setminus \\{u\\}$:\n   $$dp[S][u] = \\min_{v \\in S \\setminus \\{u\\}} \\{ dp[S \\setminus \\{u\\}][v] + \\text{dist}(v, u) \\}$$\n   There are $|S|-1 \\le n$ choices for $v$.\n3. **Total Work:** $\\sum_{S} \\sum_{u \\in S} |S| = \\Theta(n^2 2^n)$.\n4. Thus, space is $\\Theta(n 2^n)$ and time is $\\Theta(n^2 2^n)$.",
