    "explanation": "**3-SAT to CLIQUE Reduction Proof:**\n1. **Vertex Set:** For each clause $C_r = (l_{r1} \\lor l_{r2} \\lor l_{r3})$, create a triple of vertices $v_{r1}, v_{r2}, v_{r3}$. Total vertices $|V| = 3k$.\n2. **Edge Set:** Put an undirected edge between $v_{ri}$ and $v_{sj}$ if and only if:\n   - $r \\ne s$ (they belong to different clauses), AND\n   - $l_{ri} \\ne \\neg l_{sj}$ (the literals are consistent / not contradictory).\n3. **Forward Direction ($\\implies$):** If $\\phi$ is satisfiable, pick one true literal from each of the $k$ clauses. The corresponding $k$ vertices belong to different clauses and contain no contradictory literals, so every pair is connected by an edge $\\implies$ forms a clique of size $k$.\n4. **Backward Direction ($\\impliedby$):** If $G$ has a clique of size $k$, it must pick exactly one vertex from each clause cluster (since no edges exist within the same clause). Assigning TRUE to these $k$ literals is consistent and satisfies all $k$ clauses.",
