    "text": "Let $G = (V, E)$ be an undirected graph and let $\\bar{G} = (V, \\bar{E})$ be its complement graph. Which of the following statements constitutes the fundamental equivalence used in the polynomial reduction between CLIQUE and VERTEX COVER?",
    "options": [
      "A subset $S \\subseteq V$ is a clique of size $k$ in $G$ if and only if $V \\setminus S$ is a vertex cover of size $|V| - k$ in $\\bar{G}$.",
      "A subset $S \\subseteq V$ is a clique of size $k$ in $G$ if and only if $S$ is a vertex cover of size $k$ in $G$.",
      "A subset $S \\subseteq V$ is a clique in $G$ if and only if $S$ is an independent set in $G$.",
      "A subset $S \\subseteq V$ is a vertex cover in $G$ if and only if $\\bar{G}$ has no edges."
    ],
