    "explanation": "**VERTEX COVER to SET COVER Reduction:**\n1. **Universe:** Let universe $U = E$ (the set of all edges in $G$).\n2. **Subsets:** For each vertex $v \\in V$, define a subset $S_v \\subseteq U$ containing all edges incident to $v$:\n   $$S_v = \\{ e \\in E \\mid v \\in e \\}$$\n3. **Equivalence:**\n   - A subset of vertices $C \\subseteq V$ covers all edges in $E$ iff the collection of subsets $\\{S_v \\mid v \\in C\\}$ satisfies $\\bigcup_{v \\in C} S_v = E = U$.\n   - Thus, $G$ has a vertex cover of size $\\le k$ if and only if universe $U$ can be covered by $\\le k$ subsets from $\\mathcal{S} = \\{S_v \\mid v \\in V\\}$.",
    "source": "GATE High-Yield Model"
