    "text": "For any undirected graph $G = (V, E)$, Gallai's Identity states that $\\alpha(G) + \\tau(G) = |V|$, where $\\alpha(G)$ is the independence number (size of maximum independent set) and $\\tau(G)$ is the vertex cover number (size of minimum vertex cover). The Petersen graph has $|V| = 10$ vertices and independence number $\\alpha(G) = 4$. What is the minimum vertex cover size $\\tau(G)$ of the Petersen graph?",
    "answer": 6,
    "explanation": "**Mathematical Proof & Calculation:**\n1. **Gallai's Theorem:** In any graph $G=(V, E)$, a set of vertices $S \\subseteq V$ is an independent set if and only if $V \\setminus S$ is a vertex cover.\n   - Maximizing $|S|$ is equivalent to minimizing $|V \\setminus S| = |V| - |S|$.\n   - Thus, $\\alpha(G) + \\tau(G) = |V|$.\n2. For the Petersen graph:\n   - Number of vertices $|V| = 10$.\n   - Independence number $\\alpha(G) = 4$.\n3. Therefore, the minimum vertex cover size is:\n   $$\\tau(G) = |V| - \\alpha(G) = 10 - 4 = 6$$.",
