    "text": "Consider a 32-bit architecture with byte-addressable memory where `sizeof(char) = 1`, `sizeof(short) = 2`, and `sizeof(int) = 4`. A variable of type $T$ must be aligned at an address that is a multiple of `sizeof(T)`. Consider the structure definition:\n```c\nstruct MyStruct {\n    char a;\n    int b;\n    char c;\n};\n```\nWhat is `sizeof(struct MyStruct)`?",
