    "type": "NAT",
    "marks": 2,
    "text": "Consider the following C program segment:\n```c\nint arr[] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};\nint *ptr1 = arr;\nint *ptr2 = arr + 3;\n```\nWhat is the integer value of the expression `*(ptr1 + 2) + (ptr2 - ptr1)`?",
    "answer": 33,
    "explanation": "### Pointer Arithmetic and Subtraction Trace:\n1. `arr` starts at base address $\\text{Base}$.\n2. `ptr1 = arr` points to `arr[0]` (value 10).\n3. `ptr2 = arr + 3` points to `arr[3]` (value 40).\n4. Evaluation of `*(ptr1 + 2)`:\n   - `ptr1 + 2` points to `arr[2]`.\n   - Dereferencing gives `arr[2] = 30`.\n5. Evaluation of `ptr2 - ptr1`:\n   - Pointer subtraction `ptr2 - ptr1` computes the number of elements of type `int` between the two pointers: `(arr + 3) - arr = 3`.\n6. Total Sum:\n   $$\\text{Sum} = 30 + 3 = 33$$\n\nThus, the result is **33**.",
