    "explanation": "### In-depth Comparison of AVL and Red-Black Trees:\n- **Statement A is TRUE**: In an AVL tree, the heights of two child subtrees differ by at most 1 (max height $\\approx 1.44 \\log_2 n$). In a Red-Black tree, the longest path can be up to twice the shortest path (max height $\\approx 2 \\log_2 n$).\n- **Statement B is TRUE**: Because AVL trees are strictly more balanced with smaller max height, search operations require fewer comparisons by a constant factor.\n- **Statement C is TRUE**: In Red-Black trees, insertion requires at most 2 rotations (and $O(\\log n)$ recolorings).\n- **Statement D is FALSE**: Deletion in an AVL tree may require up to $O(\\log n)$ rotations along the path to the root (cascading rotations). (In contrast, deletion in a Red-Black tree requires at most 3 rotations).\n\nThus, Options A, B, and C are correct.",
