    "text": "Consider the following mutually recursive C functions:\n```c\nint g(int);\n\nint f(int n) {\n    static int count = 0;\n    count += n;\n    if (n <= 1) return count;\n    return f(n - 2) + g(n - 1);\n}\n\nint g(int n) {\n    static int mult = 1;\n    mult *= 2;\n    if (n <= 1) return mult;\n    return f(n - 1) + mult;\n}\n```\nAssume operands in `+` are evaluated strictly from **left to right**. What is the value returned by the function call `f(4)`?",
    "answer": 32,
    "explanation": "### Step-by-Step Recursive Execution Trace:\n\n- `f(4)`: `count = 4`. Calls `f(2)`.\n  - `f(2)`: `count = 6`. Calls `f(0)`.\n    - `f(0)`: `count = 6`. Returns 6.\n  - In `f(2)`: Left is 6. Calls `g(1)`.\n    - `g(1)`: `mult = 2`. Returns 2.\n  - `f(2)` returns $6 + 2 = 8$.\n- In `f(4)`: Left is 8. Calls `g(3)`.\n  - `g(3)`: `mult = 4`. Calls `f(2)`.\n    - `f(2)`: `count = 8`. Calls `f(0)` $\\implies$ returns 8. Calls `g(1)`: `mult = 8` $\\implies$ returns 8. `f(2)` returns $8 + 8 = 16$.\n  - In `g(3)`: returns $16 + 8 = 24$.\n- In `f(4)`: returns $8 + 24 = 32$.",
