    "text": "Consider the 0/1 Knapsack recursive memoized solver with item weights $W = [2, 3, 4, 5]$ and maximum capacity $C = 8$:\n```c\nint memo[5][9]; // initialized to -1\n\nint knap(int i, int w) {\n    if (i == 4 || w == 0) return 0;\n    if (memo[i][w] != -1) return memo[i][w];\n    if (wt[i] > w) return memo[i][w] = knap(i + 1, w);\n    int take = val[i] + knap(i + 1, w - wt[i]);\n    int skip = knap(i + 1, w);\n    return memo[i][w] = (take > skip ? take : skip);\n}\n```\nWhat is the total number of **distinct state entries** `(i, w)` in `memo` that are populated (i.e. where `memo[i][w] != -1`) after the execution of `knap(0, 8)` completes?",
