    "text": "Consider a custom 12-bit floating-point format structured as follows:\n- Bit 11: Sign bit ($S$)\n- Bits [10:6]: 5-bit Exponent ($E$) with bias $= 15$\n- Bits [5:0]: 6-bit Fraction ($F$)\n\nThe standard IEEE 754 conventions apply (normalized numbers have implicit leading bit $1$).\n\nWhat is the exact decimal value of the bit pattern `0xC68` (hexadecimal)?",
