    "explanation": "### View Serializability Analysis:\n1. **Initial Read**: $T_1$ performs the initial read on $X$. In any view equivalent serial schedule, $T_1$ must execute first (i.e. $T_1 \\to \\dots$).\n2. **Final Write**: $T_3$ performs the final write $w_3(X)$. In any view equivalent serial schedule, $T_3$ must execute last (i.e. $\\dots \\to T_3$).\n3. This leaves only ONE possible candidate serial schedule: $T_1 \\to T_2 \\to T_3$.\n4. **Check $T_1 \\to T_2 \\to T_3$**:\n   - In $T_1 \\to T_2 \\to T_3$, write order is $w_1(X) \\to w_2(X) \\to w_3(X)$.\n   - In schedule $S$, the write order is $w_2(X) \\to w_1(X) \\to w_3(X)$.\n   - Since $w_1(X)$ overwrote $w_2(X)$ in $S$, but $w_2(X)$ would overwrite $w_1(X)$ in the serial schedule, intermediate write states differ!\n5. Therefore, $S$ is NOT view equivalent to $T_1 \\to T_2 \\to T_3$ (nor any other serial schedule).\n\nHence, $S$ is NOT view serializable (Option C)."
