    "answer": 8,
    "explanation": "Step 1: Initialize closure:\n$$(AB)^+ = \\{A, B\\}$$\n\nStep 2: Iterate over dependencies:\n1. $AB \\to C$: Since $A, B \\subseteq (AB)^+$, add $C$: $(AB)^+ = \\{A, B, C\\}$.\n2. $B \\to G$: Since $B \\subseteq (AB)^+$, add $G$: $(AB)^+ = \\{A, B, C, G\\}$.\n3. $C \\to D$: Since $C \\subseteq (AB)^+$, add $D$: $(AB)^+ = \\{A, B, C, G, D\\}$.\n4. $D \\to E$: Since $D \\subseteq (AB)^+$, add $E$: $(AB)^+ = \\{A, B, C, G, D, E\\}$.\n5. $DG \\to H$: Since $D, G \\subseteq (AB)^+$, add $H$: $(AB)^+ = \\{A, B, C, G, D, E, H\\}$.\n6. $E \\to I$: Since $E \\subseteq (AB)^+$, add $I$: $(AB)^+ = \\{A, B, C, G, D, E, H, I\\}$.\n\nStep 3: Count total attributes:\n$$(AB)^+ = \\{A, B, C, D, E, G, H, I\\}$$\nAll 8 attributes are included.\nTherefore, $|(AB)^+| = 8$.",
    "text": "Consider a relation schema $R(A, B, C, D, E, G, H, I)$ with 8 attributes and functional dependencies:\n$$F = \\{ AB \\to C, \\; C \\to D, \\; D \\to E, \\; DG \\to H, \\; B \\to G, \\; E \\to I \\}$$\n\nCompute the number of attributes in the attribute closure of $\\{A, B\\}$, denoted $|(AB)^+|$, with respect to $F$.",
    "source": "GATE Advanced Drill"
