    "explanation": "Step 1: Identify all entries in the Dirty Page Table (DPT) at the end of Analysis:\n- Page $P_1$: $\\text{recLSN} = 100$\n- Page $P_2$: $\\text{recLSN} = 110$\n- Page $P_3$: $\\text{recLSN} = 130$ (added during scan of LSN 130)\n\nStep 2: ARIES Redo rule:\nThe Redo Phase starts scanning the log at $\\min_{P \\in \\text{DPT}} (\\text{recLSN}(P))$.\n$$\\text{Redo Start LSN} = \\min(100, 110, 130) = 100$$\n\nFrom LSN 100 forward, ARIES scans every update record to repeat history (including loser transactions).\n\nAnswer is 100.",
    "text": "Continuing with the ARIES recovery process from the previous question, the Redo phase repeats history starting from the smallest $\\text{recLSN}$ among all pages present in the Dirty Page Table (DPT) at the end of the Analysis Phase.\n\nBased on the Dirty Page Table: $P_1$ has $\\text{recLSN} = 100$, $P_2$ has $\\text{recLSN} = 110$, and $P_3$ has $\\text{recLSN} = 130$.\n\nWhat is the LSN from which the ARIES Redo Phase will begin scanning and reapplying log records?",
    "source": "GATE Advanced Drill"
