    "text": "Consider Snapshot Isolation (SI) in MVCC. Suppose a bank requires that for every account holder, the sum of balances in account $A$ and account $B$ must be non-negative ($A + B \\ge 0$). Initially $A = 100$ and $B = 100$.\n\n- Transaction $T_1$ reads $A$ (100) and $B$ (100), checks $A + B - 150 \\ge 0$ (holds), and withdraws 150 from $A$ ($A \\leftarrow -50$).\n- Concurrent transaction $T_2$ reads $A$ (100) and $B$ (100), checks $A + B - 150 \\ge 0$ (holds), and withdraws 150 from $B$ ($B \\leftarrow -50$).\n\nUnder Snapshot Isolation (First-Committer-Wins rule), what is the outcome?",
