    "text": "A relation contains $N = 1,000,000$ customer tuples. Attribute `Gender` has 2 distinct values (`M`, `F`), and attribute `Region` has 4 distinct values (`North`, `South`, `East`, `West`).\n- A Bitmap Index is constructed on both attributes.\n- Each bitmap vector contains 1 bit per tuple.\n\nTo evaluate the query `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM Customers WHERE Gender = 'F' AND Region = 'North'`:\n1. The system performs a bitwise AND operation between the bitmap vector for `Gender='F'` and the bitmap vector for `Region='North'`.\n2. The system counts the number of 1-bits (population count) in the resulting vector.\n\nAssuming standard 64-bit CPU words are used to store and process the bitmap vectors, what is the MINIMUM number of 64-bit word bitwise-AND operations required to evaluate this query over all $1,000,000$ tuples?",
