    "answer": 0,
    "explanation": "Step 1: Compute original areas:\n- $\\text{MBR}_1$: $\\text{Width} = 6 - 2 = 4$, $\\text{Height} = 7 - 3 = 4 \\implies \\text{Area}_1 = 4 \\times 4 = 16$.\n- $\\text{MBR}_2$: $\\text{Width} = 14 - 10 = 4$, $\\text{Height} = 12 - 8 = 4 \\implies \\text{Area}_2 = 4 \\times 4 = 16$.\n\nStep 2: Enlargement for $\\text{MBR}_1$ with Point $P(7, 8)$:\n- New $x$-range: $[\\min(2, 7), \\max(6, 7)] = [2, 7] \\implies \\text{Width} = 5$.\n- New $y$-range: $[\\min(3, 8), \\max(7, 8)] = [3, 8] \\implies \\text{Height} = 5$.\n- New Area $= 5 \\times 5 = 25$.\n- Area Enlargement: $\\Delta \\text{Area}_1 = 25 - 16 = 9$.\n\nStep 3: Enlargement for $\\text{MBR}_2$ with Point $P(7, 8)$:\n- New $x$-range: $[\\min(10, 7), \\max(14, 7)] = [7, 14] \\implies \\text{Width} = 7$.\n- New $y$-range: $[\\min(8, 8), \\max(12, 8)] = [8, 12] \\implies \\text{Height} = 4$.\n- New Area $= 7 \\times 4 = 28$.\n- Area Enlargement: $\\Delta \\text{Area}_2 = 28 - 16 = 12$.\n\nStep 4: Selection:\nSince $\\Delta \\text{Area}_1 = 9 < \\Delta \\text{Area}_2 = 12$, the algorithm chooses $\\text{MBR}_1$.\nOption A is correct.",
    "text": "In an R-Tree index for 2D spatial objects, a leaf node contains two Minimum Bounding Rectangles (MBRs):\n- $\\text{MBR}_1$: $[x_{\\min}=2, x_{\\max}=6] \\times [y_{\\min}=3, y_{\\max}=7]$\n- $\\text{MBR}_2$: $[x_{\\min}=10, x_{\\max}=14] \\times [y_{\\min}=8, y_{\\max}=12]$\n\nA new 2D point object $P(7, 8)$ is to be inserted. The R-Tree insertion algorithm chooses the MBR whose enlargement in area is minimized (least area enlargement $\\Delta \\text{Area}$).\n\nWhat are the area enlargements $\\Delta \\text{Area}_1$ and $\\Delta \\text{Area}_2$ for $\\text{MBR}_1$ and $\\text{MBR}_2$ respectively, and which MBR is chosen?",
