    "text": "Let $L_k = \\{w \\in \\{0, 1\\}^* \\mid \\text{the } k\\text{-th symbol from the right end of } w \\text{ is } 1\\}$. It is well known that any DFA recognizing $L_k$ requires at least $2^k$ states, whereas an NFA requires $k+1$ states. Now consider an Alternating Finite Automaton (AFA) recognizing $L_k^{rev} = \\{w \\in \\{0, 1\\}^* \\mid \\text{the } k\\text{-th symbol from the left end of } w \\text{ is } 1\\}$. What is the state complexity (minimum number of states) required by an AFA to recognize the intersection $L = \\bigcap_{i=1}^m L_{k_i}$ where each $L_{k_i}$ checks the $k_i$-th symbol from the right?",
