    "text": "Let $L = \\{w \\in \\{0, 1\\}^* \\mid |w| \\equiv 0 \\pmod 6 \\text{ and } n_1(w) \\equiv 0 \\pmod 4\\}$, where $|w|$ is the length of $w$ and $n_1(w)$ is the number of 1s in $w$. What is the exact number of equivalence classes of the Myhill-Nerode relation $R_L$ for language $L$?",
    "source": "GATE High-Yield Model",
