    "type": "NAT",
    "explanation": "When processing a binary string $w$ from left to right, appending bit $b \\in \\{0, 1\\}$ updates the integer value as:\n$$\\text{val}(wb) = 2 \\cdot \\text{val}(w) + b$$\nTaking modulo 5:\n$$(\\text{val}(wb) \\bmod 5) = (2 \\cdot (\\text{val}(w) \\bmod 5) + b) \\bmod 5$$\nThis gives 5 states corresponding to remainders $\\{0, 1, 2, 3, 4\\} \\pmod 5$.\n\nLet's verify pairwise distinguishability of remainders $r_1 \\ne r_2 \\in \\{0, 1, 2, 3, 4\\}$:\n- From state $r$, appending suffix $z$ of length $k$ produces remainder $(r \\cdot 2^k + \\text{val}(z)) \\bmod 5$.\n- Since $\\gcd(2, 5) = 1$, the map $r \\mapsto r \\cdot 2^k \\bmod 5$ is a bijection on $\\mathbb{Z}_5$.\n- Choosing $\\text{val}(z) = (-r_1 \\cdot 2^k) \\bmod 5$ makes the first state reach remainder $0$ (accepting), while the second state reaches $(r_2 - r_1) 2^k \\not\\equiv 0 \\pmod 5$ (non-accepting).\nThus, all 5 states are pairwise distinguishable, so the minimal DFA has exactly 5 states.",
