    "explanation": "### Token Breakdown by Lexical Analyzer:\nIn C, tokens are the smallest individual units recognized by the lexical analyzer.\n1. `printf` (identifier / function name)\n2. `(` (punctuation / left parenthesis)\n3. `\"i = %d, &i = %x\"` (string literal / single token)\n4. `,` (comma separator)\n5. `i` (identifier)\n6. `,` (comma separator)\n7. `&` (address-of operator)\n8. `i` (identifier)\n9. `)` (punctuation / right parenthesis)\n10. `;` (semicolon statement terminator)\n\nTotal number of tokens = **10**.\n\nHence, the correct option is (C)."
