    "explanation": "### Three-Address Code Data Structures:\n1. **Quadruples**: Has 4 fields (`op`, `arg1`, `arg2`, `result`). Explicitly names temporary variables.\n2. **Triples**: Has 3 fields (`op`, `arg1`, `arg2`). Refers to temporary results by their table position `(i)`. Moving statements requires updating all position references.\n3. **Indirect Triples**: Contains an array of triples, along with a separate array of **pointers** listing the execution order of the triples. Statement reordering during optimization is achieved simply by reordering the pointer array without modifying the underlying triples.\n\nHence, the correct option is (A) Indirect Triples."
