    "explanation": "### Static vs Dynamic Scoping Analysis:\n1. **Static (Lexical) Scoping**:\n   - Free identifier references are resolved in the **lexical enclosing block** where procedure `P` is defined.\n   - `P` is defined directly in `main`. The global `x` in `main` has value $5$.\n   - Thus, under Static Scoping, `P` prints **5**.\n2. **Dynamic Scoping**:\n   - Free identifier references are resolved along the dynamic call stack at runtime.\n   - `main` calls `Q`, and `Q` defines a local `x = 10` before calling `P`.\n   - The most recent active activation record with binding for `x` is `Q`'s activation record.\n   - Thus, under Dynamic Scoping, `P` prints **10**.\n\nValues printed: **5 and 10** (Option A)."
