    "explanation": "### Short-Circuit Jump Generation:\n1. `if a < b goto L_TRUE` (First conditional jump: if true, skips the rest of the $||$ condition).\n2. If false, evaluate `c < d && e < f`:\n   - `if c >= d goto L_FALSE` (Second conditional jump: if false, short-circuits the $\\&\\&$).\n   - `if e < f goto L_TRUE` (Third conditional jump: evaluates final condition).\n3. Total number of conditional jumps = **3**.\n\nOption (A) is correct."
