    "explanation": "Let us evaluate the sub-expressions step-by-step:\n\n1. $E_1: (a < b)$\n   - $100: \\mathbf{if} \\; a < b \\; \\mathbf{goto} \\; \\_$\n   - $101: \\mathbf{goto} \\; \\_$\n   - $E_1.\\textit{truelist} = \\{100\\}, \\; E_1.\\textit{falselist} = \\{101\\}$.\n\n2. $E_2: (c > d)$\n   - $102: \\mathbf{if} \\; c > d \\; \\mathbf{goto} \\; \\_$\n   - $103: \\mathbf{goto} \\; \\_$\n   - $E_2.\\textit{truelist} = \\{102\\}, \\; E_2.\\textit{falselist} = \\{103\\}$.\n\n3. $E_3: (e == f)$\n   - $104: \\mathbf{if} \\; e == f \\; \\mathbf{goto} \\; \\_$\n   - $105: \\mathbf{goto} \\; \\_$\n   - $E_3.\\textit{truelist} = \\{104\\}, \\; E_3.\\textit{falselist} = \\{105\\}$.\n\n4. $E_{23} = E_2 \\; \\mathbf{and} \\; M_1 \\; E_3$ where marker $M_1$ is at instruction 104:\n   - $\\textit{backpatch}(E_2.\\textit{truelist}, 104) \\implies$ line 102 jumps to 104.\n   - $E_{23}.\\textit{truelist} = E_3.\\textit{truelist} = \\{104\\}$.\n   - $E_{23}.\\textit{falselist} = \\textit{merge}(E_2.\\textit{falselist}, E_3.\\textit{falselist}) = \\{103, 105\\}$.\n\n5. $E = E_1 \\; \\mathbf{or} \\; M_2 \\; E_{23}$ where marker $M_2$ is at instruction 102:\n   - $\\textit{backpatch}(E_1.\\textit{falselist}, 102) \\implies$ line 101 jumps to 102.\n   - $E.\\textit{truelist} = \\textit{merge}(E_1.\\textit{truelist}, E_{23}.\\textit{truelist}) = \\{100, 104\\}$.\n   - $E.\\textit{falselist} = E_{23}.\\textit{falselist} = \\{103, 105\\}$.\n\nThus, $E.\\textit{truelist} = \\{100, 104\\}$ and $E.\\textit{falselist} = \\{103, 105\\}$. Option (A) (index 0) is correct.",
    "text": "Consider the translation of the following boolean expression using standard backpatching rules (where each relational test emits a conditional jump and an unconditional jump):\n$$E: \\quad (a < b) \\; \\mathbf{or} \\; ((c > d) \\; \\mathbf{and} \\; (e == f))$$\nAssume the generated 3-address code instructions start at instruction address 100 as follows:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n100:& \\; \\mathbf{if} \\; a < b \\; \\mathbf{goto} \\; \\_ \\\\\n101:& \\; \\mathbf{goto} \\; \\_ \\\\\n102:& \\; \\mathbf{if} \\; c > d \\; \\mathbf{goto} \\; \\_ \\\\\n103:& \\; \\mathbf{goto} \\; \\_ \\\\\n104:& \\; \\mathbf{if} \\; e == f \\; \\mathbf{goto} \\; \\_ \\\\\n105:& \\; \\mathbf{goto} \\; \\_\n\\end{aligned}$$\nLet $E.\\textit{truelist}$ and $E.\\textit{falselist}$ be the lists of instruction addresses to be backpatched for true and false exits of $E$, respectively.\nWhich of the following represents the correct lists $(E.\\textit{truelist}, E.\\textit{falselist})$?",
