    "explanation": "Let us list all emitted three-address instructions sequentially:\n\n1. Start of `while` at instruction $L_0$:\n   - $C_1$ evaluated: (2 instructions)\n     - $I_1$: `if C1 goto L_then`\n     - $I_2$: `goto L_exit` (in $C_1.falselist$, backpatched to $L_{end}$)\n2. Inside loop body (target of $C_1.truelist$ at $I_3$):\n   - $C_2$ evaluated: (2 instructions)\n     - $I_3$: `if C2 goto L_S1`\n     - $I_4$: `goto L_S2` (in $C_2.falselist$)\n3. $S_1$ block (target of $C_2.truelist$ at $I_5$):\n   - $I_5, I_6, I_7$: 3 assignment instructions for $S_1$\n   - $I_8$: `goto L_while_end` (unconditional jump to bypass $S_2$)\n4. $S_2$ block (target of $C_2.falselist$ at $I_9$):\n   - $I_9, I_{10}$: 2 assignment instructions for $S_2$\n5. Loop back instruction:\n   - $I_{11}$: `goto L_0` (jumps back to $C_1$ start at $I_1$)\n\nWait, let's recount:\n- $C_1$: 2 instructions\n- $C_2$: 2 instructions\n- $S_1$: 3 instructions\n- Jump over $S_2$: 1 instruction\n- $S_2$: 2 instructions\n- Jump to loop header: 1 instruction\nTotal = $2 + 2 + 3 + 1 + 2 + 1 = 11$ instructions.\nWait, if the loop back jump is merged with the fallthrough of $S_2$, then $I_8$ (jump after $S_1$) jumps to $I_{11}$ (`goto L_0`), or directly to $L_0$.\nTotal generated instructions = 11.",
    "text": "Consider translating the nested control structure:\n$$\\mathbf{while} \\; (C_1) \\; \\{ \\; \\mathbf{if} \\; (C_2) \\; S_1; \\; \\mathbf{else} \\; S_2; \\; \\}$$\ninto three-address code using syntax-directed translation with backpatching.\nAssume:\n- Evaluating $C_1$ produces 2 instructions (1 conditional jump, 1 unconditional jump).\n- Evaluating $C_2$ produces 2 instructions.\n- Statement $S_1$ produces 3 assignment instructions.\n- Statement $S_2$ produces 2 assignment instructions.\n- Standard unconditional jumps are emitted to bypass `else` branch and to loop back to the start of `while`.\nCalculate the total number of three-address code instructions generated for this entire construct.",
