    "text": "Consider the L-attributed SDD for calculating decimal value from a binary fractional string:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\nS &\\to L . L_1 & \\{ S.val &= L.val + L_1.val; \\; L_1.pos = -1 \\} \\\\\nL &\\to B \\; L_1 & \\{ L.val &= B.val * 2^{L_1.len} + L_1.val; \\; L.len = L_1.len + 1 \\} \\\\\nL &\\to \\epsilon & \\{ L.val &= 0; \\; L.len = 0 \\} \\\\\nL_1 &\\to B \\; L_2 & \\{ L_1.val &= B.val * 2^{L_1.pos} + L_2.val; \\; L_2.pos = L_1.pos - 1 \\} \\\\\nL_1 &\\to \\epsilon & \\{ L_1.val &= 0 \\} \\\\\nB &\\to 0 & \\{ B.val &= 0 \\} \\\\\nB &\\to 1 & \\{ B.val &= 1 \\}\n\\end{aligned}$$\nFor the input string $w = 11.011$, what is the computed value $S.val$ expressed as a decimal float multiplied by 8 (i.e., calculate $8 \\times S.val$)?",
