    "explanation": "Let us examine each statement:\n- **Statement A is correct**: $env$ is passed from parent to children ($P \\to B$, $B \\to D$) and from left sibling to right sibling ($D \\to S$), which is an inherited attribute.\n- **Statement B is correct**: All inherited attributes depend only on parent attributes or left siblings, satisfying L-attributed grammar rules.\n- **Statement C is INCORRECT**: An S-attributed definition contains *only* synthesized attributes. Since this grammar uses inherited attributes ($env$), it is NOT S-attributed.\n- **Statement D is correct**: $\\text{newEnv}(B.env)$ constructs a child scope linked to parent scope $B.env$.\n\nHence, Statement C is the incorrect statement. Option (C) (index 2) is correct.",
