    "type": "NAT",
    "answer": 0,
    "explanation": "Let us compute the backward analysis:\n\n1. For $B_2$ and $B_3$:\n   - $\\text{OUT}[B_2] = \\text{IN}[\\text{Exit}] = \\emptyset \\implies \\text{IN}[B_2] = \\text{USED}[B_2] = \\{a+b, c*d\\}$.\n   - $\\text{OUT}[B_3] = \\text{IN}[\\text{Exit}] = \\emptyset \\implies \\text{IN}[B_3] = \\text{USED}[B_3] = \\{a+b, e-f\\}$.\n\n2. For $B_1$:\n   - $\\text{OUT}[B_1] = \\text{IN}[B_2] \\cap \\text{IN}[B_3] = \\{a+b, c*d\\} \\cap \\{a+b, e-f\\} = \\{a+b\\}$.\n   - $\\text{IN}[B_1] = \\text{USED}[B_1] \\cup (\\text{OUT}[B_1] - \\text{KILL}[B_1]) = \\emptyset \\cup (\\{a+b\\} - \\{a+b\\}) = \\emptyset$.\n\nThus, $|\\text{IN}[B_1]| = 0$.",
    "text": "Very Busy Expressions analysis is a backward MUST dataflow framework used for code hoisting.\nDataflow equations:\n$$\\text{OUT}[B] = \\bigcap_{S \\in \\text{succ}(B)} \\text{IN}[S], \\quad \\text{IN}[B] = \\text{USED}[B] \\cup (\\text{OUT}[B] - \\text{KILL}[B])$$\nwith $\\text{IN}[\\text{Exit}] = \\emptyset$ and $\\text{IN}[B] = \\mathcal{U}$ initially for all $B \\neq \\text{Exit}$.\nConsider a CFG where:\n- Block $B_1$ has successors $B_2$ and $B_3$.\n- $\\text{USED}[B_2] = \\{a+b, \\; c*d\\}, \\quad \\text{KILL}[B_2] = \\{e-f\\}$.\n- $\\text{USED}[B_3] = \\{a+b, \\; e-f\\}, \\quad \\text{KILL}[B_3] = \\{c*d\\}$.\n- Both $B_2$ and $B_3$ lead to $\\text{Exit}$.\n- $\\text{USED}[B_1] = \\emptyset, \\quad \\text{KILL}[B_1] = \\{a+b\\}$.\nHow many expressions are very busy at the entry of $B_1$, i.e., calculate $|\\text{IN}[B_1]|$?",
