    "explanation": "In instruction selection theory:\n- **Maximal Munch** is a greedy top-down algorithm that selects the largest matching tile at the current root. Because it makes locally greedy choices without considering global cost tradeoffs, it can produce sub-optimal code.\n- **Dynamic Programming (Aho-Johnson)** works bottom-up, computing optimal costs for each non-terminal at every tree node, guaranteeing a globally minimum cost tiling in linear $O(N)$ time.\n\nOption (B) (index 1) is correct.",
