    "explanation": "Let us compute the Iterated Dominance Frontier $IDF(\\mathcal{S})$ for $\\mathcal{S} = \\{B_2, B_5\\}$:\n\n1. Initial definition set $S_0 = \\{B_2, B_5\\}$.\n2. Step 1: $DF(S_0) = DF(B_2) \\cup DF(B_5) = \\{B_4\\} \\cup \\{B_6\\} = \\{B_4, B_6\\}$.\n   - Add $B_4$ and $B_6$ to the frontier set: $S_1 = \\{B_2, B_5, B_4, B_6\\}$.\n3. Step 2: Compute $DF$ of newly added nodes $\\{B_4, B_6\\}$:\n   - $DF(B_4) = \\{B_7\\}$.\n   - $DF(B_6) = \\{B_4\\}$ (already included).\n   - Add $B_7$: $S_2 = \\{B_2, B_5, B_4, B_6, B_7\\}$.\n4. Step 3: Compute $DF(B_7) = \\emptyset$.\n   - No new nodes are added. Fixed point reached!\n5. The set of blocks requiring a $\\phi$-function for $x$ is $IDF(\\{B_2, B_5\\}) = \\{B_4, B_6, B_7\\}$.\n\nThus, exactly 3 $\\phi$-functions are inserted.",
    "text": "In minimal SSA form construction, $\\phi$-functions for variable $v$ are placed at the Iterated Dominance Frontier $IDF(\\mathcal{S})$, where $\\mathcal{S}$ is the set of basic blocks containing assignment definitions to $v$.\nConsider a CFG with 7 blocks where $DF$ sets are:\n- $DF(B_1) = \\emptyset$\n- $DF(B_2) = \\{B_4\\}$\n- $DF(B_3) = \\{B_4\\}$\n- $DF(B_4) = \\{B_7\\}$\n- $DF(B_5) = \\{B_6\\}$\n- $DF(B_6) = \\{B_4\\}$\n- $DF(B_7) = \\emptyset$\nSuppose variable $x$ is defined only in blocks $\\mathcal{S} = \\{B_2, B_5\\}$.\nHow many $\\phi$-functions for variable $x$ will be inserted across the entire CFG in minimal SSA form?",
