    "explanation": "Let us evaluate the number of $\\phi$-functions for each variable under Pruned SSA:\n\n1. For $v_1$: Since $v_1$ is local, it is never live on entry to any other block $\\implies 0$ $\\phi$-functions in Pruned SSA.\n2. For $v_2$: Live on entry to all 3 blocks in $IDF(v_2) \\implies 3$ $\\phi$-functions.\n3. For $v_3$: Out of 2 blocks in $IDF(v_3)$, $v_3$ is live on entry to 1 block $\\implies 1$ $\\phi$-function.\n4. For $v_4$: Dead on entry to both blocks in $IDF(v_4) \\implies 0$ $\\phi$-functions.\n\nTotal $\\phi$-functions in Pruned SSA = $0 + 3 + 1 + 0 = 4$.",
    "text": "In SSA construction:\n- **Minimal SSA** places $\\phi$-functions at all nodes in $IDF(\\mathcal{S})$.\n- **Semi-Pruned SSA** omits $\\phi$-functions for local variables (variables not live across any basic block boundary).\n- **Pruned SSA** places $\\phi$-functions at node $B \\in IDF(\\mathcal{S})$ only if the variable is live on entry to $B$ ($\\text{IN}[B]$).\nSuppose a function has 4 variables $\\{v_1, v_2, v_3, v_4\\}$ where:\n- $v_1$ is local to a single block (not live across boundaries), but has 2 definitions in that block ($|IDF| = 1$).\n- $v_2$ is global, with $|IDF| = 3$, and is live on entry to all 3 blocks.\n- $v_3$ is global, with $|IDF| = 2$, but is dead on entry to 1 of the 2 blocks.\n- $v_4$ is global, with $|IDF| = 2$, and is dead on entry to both blocks.\nCalculate the total number of $\\phi$-functions inserted in **Pruned SSA form** across all 4 variables.",
