    "id": "dl-adv-011",
    "subject": "Digital Logic",
    "chapterId": "c-dl-setup-hold-time",
    "type": "NAT",
    "marks": 2,
    "text": "A negative edge-triggered flip-flop $FF_1$ drives a positive edge-triggered flip-flop $FF_2$ with a common $50\\%$ duty cycle clock of frequency $f = 100\\text{ MHz}$ ($T_{clk} = 10\\text{ ns}$). \n- $FF_1$ clock-to-Q delay: $t_{cq1} = 1.5\\text{ ns}$\n- $FF_2$ setup time: $t_{setup2} = 1.1\\text{ ns}$\n- Clock skew is zero.\n\nWhat is the **maximum combinational logic delay** $t_{comb,\\max}$ (in ns) permissible between $FF_1$ and $FF_2$?",
    "answer": 2.4,
    "explanation": "**Step-by-step Half-Cycle Setup Analysis:**\n\n1. **Launch and Capture Edge Identification:**\n   - $FF_1$ launches data on the **negative (falling) edge** of the clock at $t = T_{clk}/2 = 5.0\\text{ ns}$.\n   - $FF_2$ captures data on the very next **positive (rising) edge** at $t = T_{clk} = 10.0\\text{ ns}$.\n   - Total time available between launch and capture is half a clock period: $T_{available} = T_{clk} / 2 = 5.0\\text{ ns}$.\n\n2. **Setup Constraint Equation:**\n   $$t_{cq1} + t_{comb,\\max} + t_{setup2} \\le \\frac{T_{clk}}{2}$$\n\n3. **Calculation:**\n   $$1.5\\text{ ns} + t_{comb,\\max} + 1.1\\text{ ns} \\le 5.0\\text{ ns}$$\n   $$t_{comb,\\max} \\le 5.0 - 2.6 = 2.4\\text{ ns}$$\n\nThus, the maximum combinational delay is **2.4 ns**.",
    "source": "GATE Advanced Drill",
    "difficulty": 3
