    "explanation": "A linear extension of a poset $P = (X, \\le)$ is a total order $(X, \\le_T)$ that preserves all relations in $P$.\nHere $X$ has size $3 + 3 = 6$.\nA total order must interleave the 3 elements of chain $A = \\{a_1 < a_2 < a_3\\}$ and the 3 elements of chain $B = \\{b_1 < b_2 < b_3\\}$.\nSince the relative order within $A$ and within $B$ is completely fixed, specifying a linear extension is equivalent to choosing which 3 positions out of the 6 total positions in the sequence are occupied by elements of $A$ (in their unique order $a_1, a_2, a_3$). The remaining 3 positions are filled by $b_1, b_2, b_3$.\nTherefore, the number of linear extensions is:\n$$\\binom{6}{3} = \\frac{6 \\times 5 \\times 4}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = 20.$$",
