    "explanation": "Let us find the cycle index of $D_4$ acting on the 4 cells:\n1. Identity (1): $z_1^4$ (fixes all $2^4 = 16$ colorings)\n2. $90^\\circ$ and $270^\\circ$ rotations (2): 1 cycle of 4 $\\implies z_4^1$ (each fixes $2^1 = 2$ colorings)\n3. $180^\\circ$ rotation (1): 2 cycles of 2 $\\implies z_2^2$ (fixes $2^2 = 4$ colorings)\n4. 2 axis reflections (horizontal & vertical) (2): 2 cycles of 2 $\\implies z_2^2$ (each fixes $2^2 = 4$ colorings)\n5. 2 diagonal reflections (2): 2 cycles of 1 and 1 cycle of 2 $\\implies z_1^2 z_2^1$ (each fixes $2^3 = 8$ colorings)\n\nCycle index $Z(D_4) = \\frac{1}{8} [z_1^4 + 2 z_4 + 3 z_2^2 + 2 z_1^2 z_2]$.\nSubstitute $z_i = 2$:\n$$N = \\frac{1}{8} [2^4 + 2(2^1) + 3(2^2) + 2(2^2 \\cdot 2)]$$\n$$N = \\frac{1}{8} [16 + 4 + 12 + 16] = \\frac{1}{8} [48] = 6.$$\nThus, there are exactly 6 distinct colorings.",
