    "answer": 35,
    "explanation": "We use the recurrence relation $\\left[ \\begin{matrix} n \\\\ k \\end{matrix} \\right] = (n-1) \\left[ \\begin{matrix} n-1 \\\\ k \\end{matrix} \\right] + \\left[ \\begin{matrix} n-1 \\\\ k-1 \\end{matrix} \\right]$.\nLet us construct the table row by row:\n- Row 1: [1, 1] = 1\n- Row 2: [2, 1] = 1, [2, 2] = 1\n- Row 3:\n  - [3, 1] = 2\n  - [3, 2] = 2(1) + 1 = 3\n  - [3, 3] = 1\n- Row 4:\n  - [4, 1] = 6\n  - [4, 2] = 3(3) + 2 = 11\n  - [4, 3] = 3(1) + 3 = 6\n  - [4, 4] = 1\n- Row 5:\n  - $\\left[ \\begin{matrix} 5 \\\\ 3 \\end{matrix} \\right] = 4 \\left[ \\begin{matrix} 4 \\\\ 3 \\end{matrix} \\right] + \\left[ \\begin{matrix} 4 \\\\ 2 \\end{matrix} \\right] = 4(6) + 11 = 24 + 11 = 35$.\n\nAlternatively, cycles in $S_5$ with 3 cycles can be:\n1. Type $(3, 1, 1)$: $\\binom{5}{3} \\times (3-1)! = 10 \\times 2 = 20$.\n2. Type $(2, 2, 1)$: $\\frac{1}{2!} \\binom{5}{2} \\binom{3}{2} \\times 1! \\times 1! = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 3 = 15$.\nTotal $= 20 + 15 = 35$.",
    "difficulty": 3,
    "text": "The unsigned Stirling numbers of the first kind $\\left[ \\begin{matrix} n \\\\ k \\end{matrix} \\right]$ count the number of permutations of $n$ elements with exactly $k$ disjoint cycles. Compute the exact value of $\\left[ \\begin{matrix} 5 \\\\ 3 \\end{matrix} \\right]$.",
