    "explanation": "Step 1: Find the image $\\mathrm{Im}(\\phi)$:\n- The generator 1 of $\\mathbb{Z}_{36}$ maps to $12 \\in \\mathbb{Z}_{48}$.\n- The order of $12$ in the additive group $(\\mathbb{Z}_{48}, +)$ is:\n  $$\\operatorname{ord}(12) = \\frac{48}{\\gcd(12, 48)} = \\frac{48}{12} = 4.$$\n- Therefore, the subgroup $\\mathrm{Im}(\\phi) = \\langle 12 \\rangle \\le \\mathbb{Z}_{48}$ has order 4.\n\nStep 2: Apply the First Isomorphism Theorem for groups:\n$$\\mathbb{Z}_{36} / \\ker(\\phi) \\cong \\mathrm{Im}(\\phi)$$\n$$|\\mathbb{Z}_{36} / \\ker(\\phi)| = |\\mathrm{Im}(\\phi)| = 4$$\n$$\\frac{|\\mathbb{Z}_{36}|}{|\\ker(\\phi)|} = 4 \\implies |\\ker(\\phi)| = \\frac{36}{4} = 9.$$\nThus, the kernel contains exactly 9 elements (specifically, multiples of 4: $\\{0, 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32\\}$).",
